From: keptn42 <keptn42@noreply.codeberg.org>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:43:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] moe_gemm_q run-aligned form: the first pass's weight at
 the map read (R4D_MOE_PF2 64)

In the run-aligned form the map entry names the block's expert, yet the
weight loads wait behind the token load, a barrier, the live count and the
table entry. Part 64 issues the rows and the live count first, then the
table entries and the first pass's weight through the uniform global base,
all unconditional, so the weight stays in flight while the tokens arrive.
The same bytes go to the same registers and LDS slots: bit-identical.
